  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As per given figures, two springs of spring constants <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> are connected to mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the period of oscillation in figure (a) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, then the period of oscillation in figure (b) will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0059_88800af85209.jpg\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 283px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0059_88800af85209.jpg\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 283px;\" /></p><p>In figure (a), the springs are connected in series. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, the time period</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>In&nbsp;figure (b), the springs are connected in parallel. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>K</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, the time period</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Now,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}